  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Inline Highlight\n\nA sentence where one word is picked out by fading from the base colour to an accent colour.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 3 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- One word in a sentence deserves the eye: a product name, a number, a key phrase.\n- A quiet emphasis that does not move the layout.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The emphasis should look hand-drawn: use marker-highlight.\n- Several words should be picked out in turn: use a caption highlight.\n\nVariables:\n- before (string): Before, default \"Ship faster with \"\n- highlight (string): Highlight, default \"motion\"\n- after (string): After, default \".\"\n- base_color (color): Base color, default \"#171717\"\n- highlight_color (color): Highlight color, default \"#ff5e3a\"\n- font_size (number, 12-240): Font size, default 72\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"600\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Inline Highlight\n\n  A sentence where one word is picked out by fading from the base colour to an accent colour.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/inline-highlight/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"inline-highlight\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"3\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"before\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Before\", \"description\": \"Text before the highlighted word.\", \"default\": \"Ship faster with \"},\n    {\"id\": \"highlight\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Highlight\", \"description\": \"The word that changes colour.\", \"default\": \"motion\"},\n    {\"id\": \"after\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"After\", \"description\": \"Text after the highlighted word.\", \"default\": \".\"},\n    {\"id\": \"base_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Base color\", \"description\": \"Color of the sentence.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"highlight_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Highlight color\", \"description\": \"Color the highlighted word fades to.\", \"default\": \"#ff5e3a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 72, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 240, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"600\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Inline Highlight</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\" />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        #root { background: #ffffff; font-family: Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif; }\n        .ih-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .ih-line { letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1.2; text-align: center; max-width: 92%; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"inline-highlight\" data-duration=\"3\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"ih-clip\" class=\"ih-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"3\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"ih-line\" class=\"ih-line\" role=\"img\"><span id=\"ih-before\"></span><span id=\"ih-hl\"></span><span id=\"ih-after\"></span></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 to 1, rest at 0 velocity (mass, stiffness, damping), at `frame` of 30 fps.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass, k = cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            var TOTAL = 3;\n            var FRAMES = Math.round(TOTAL * 30);\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function frameNow() { return Math.round(clock.frame * 1000) / 1000; }\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: FRAMES, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(frameNow()); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"inline-highlight\"] = tl;\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            function fit(el, size, frac, hfrac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxW = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              var maxH = Math.max(1, root.clientHeight * (hfrac || 0.9));\n              var k = Math.min(1, maxW / Math.max(1, el.scrollWidth), maxH / Math.max(1, el.scrollHeight));\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(8, size * k); el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n\n\n            var before = typeof vars.before === \"string\" ? vars.before : \"Ship faster with \";\n            var hl = str(vars.highlight, \"motion\");\n            var after = typeof vars.after === \"string\" ? vars.after : \".\";\n            var size = num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 240), speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var baseC = str(vars.base_color, \"#171717\"), hiC = str(vars.highlight_color, \"#ff5e3a\");\n            function rgb(c) {\n              var m = /^#?([0-9a-f]{3}|[0-9a-f]{6})$/i.exec(c.trim());\n              if (!m) return [23, 23, 23];\n              var h = m[1].length === 3 ? m[1].replace(/./g, \"$&$&\") : m[1];\n              return [parseInt(h.slice(0, 2), 16), parseInt(h.slice(2, 4), 16), parseInt(h.slice(4, 6), 16)];\n            }\n            var c0 = rgb(baseC), c1 = rgb(hiC);\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"ih-line\"), hlEl = document.getElementById(\"ih-hl\");\n            document.getElementById(\"ih-before\").textContent = before;\n            hlEl.textContent = hl;\n            document.getElementById(\"ih-after\").textContent = after;\n            line.style.color = baseC;\n            line.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"600\");\n            line.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", before + hl + after);\n            fit(line, size, 0.9); onFonts(function () { fit(line, size, 0.9); });\n            start(function (raw) {\n              var f = raw * speed;\n              var p = ip(f, FRAMES * 0.2, FRAMES * 0.7, 0, 1);\n              var c = c0.map(function (v, i) { return Math.round(v + (c1[i] - v) * p); });\n              hlEl.style.color = \"rgb(\" + c.join(\",\") + \")\";\n            });\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
